  "raw_text": "152\n\nNina m\nâ\nkaia\n \n(Nina makaia)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto name, to be named, to be called, to give a name\n \n/ nombrar, ser nombrado, ser\n\nllamado, dar un nombre\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb16\n):\n \nJob nina mâki kan\n \n–\n \n(He) was being called Job\n \n/ (Él) se llamaba Job)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh14\n):\n \nGâd selp ai nina Jehova makan ba\n \n–\n \nGod gave himself the name Jehovah\n \n/ Dios se dio el nombre de Jehová)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n12/18\n):\n \nDîa\n \nmuni Saulo ra Pal nina sin m\nâkisa?\n \n–\n \nWhy is Saul also called Paul?\n \n/ ¿Por qué Sa\nu\nl\no\n \ntambién se\n\nllama Pablo?\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb68\n):\n \nElisabet mayam ba, luhpa kum baikbia, bara ai nina Jan mâkma\n \n–\n \nElizabeth your wife will give\n \nbirth to a child\n\nand you will name (him) John\n \n/ Elisabet tu esposa dará a luz a un hijo y tú lo llamarás Juan\n)\n\nMakupaia\n \n(v-See also/ Ver también:\n \nAimakupaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto bow, to face downward, to stoop, to turn over\n \n/ inclinarse, mirar\nhacia abajo, agacharse, darse vuelta\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb-60\n):\n \nNabucodonosor Daniel mawan ra ai lula kriki ai lal makupi bara win:...\n \n–\n \nNebuchadnezzar kneeling down in front of\nDaniel with his head facing downward said: ...\n \n/ Nabucodonosor se arrodilló frente a Daniel con la cabeza hacia abajo y dijo: ...)\n\nMala\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nsharp\n \n(the edge of a knife or machete) / afilado (el borde de un cuchillo o machete)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Hibru Nani 4:12\n):\n \nsord mala napa wal\n \n–\n \nsword with sharp teeth\n \n/ espada con dientes afilados)\n\nMala daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto sharpen\n \n/ afilar\n\nMalaquías\n \n(Malaquias)\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \nMalakai\n-bw,dba\n;\n \nMalaquias\n-dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nMalachi\n \n(Bible book) / Malaquías (libro bíblico)\n\nMama\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmama, mother\n \n/ mama, madre\n \n(\nS\nee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nYapti\n)\n\n(Construct:\n \nMamiki\n;\n \nMamikam\n;\n \nMamika\n)\n\nMaman\ng\nkra\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nMamankra\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nsower, planter\n \n/ sembrador, plantador\n\nInsla mamangkra\n \n(a/t:\n \nInsla mamankra\n-\nbh,my\n)\n \n(see/ver:\n \nMangkaia\n)\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nfarmer\n \n/ finquero\n\nMamaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto knit, to weave, to darn, to mend\n \n/ tejer, zurcir\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPitbaia\n)\n\nMamdiskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto shade you, to overshadow you\n \n/ sombrearte, eclipsararte\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMadiskaia\n \n–\n \nto\nshade, to overshadow\n \n/ sombrear, eclipsar)\n\nMamkabaia\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMakabaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto ask of you, to beg of you, to petition you, to demand of you, to\nimplore to you, to beseech you, to pray to you\n \n/ pedirte, rogarte, implorarte, suplicarte, rezarte\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nJehova, mamkabisna...\n \n–\n \nJehovah, I ask of you...\n \n/ Jehová, te pido ...)\n\nMamkabi walaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ask a question to you\n \n/ hacerte una pregunta\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n11/20\n):\n \nUplika ba diara kum mamkabi walbia kaka, …\n \n–\n \nIf the person asks you a question, …\n \n/ Si la persona te\n\nhace una pregunta, ...\n)\n\nMamkabi walanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nquestion for you\n \n/ una pregunta para ti\n\nMamkabi wals\n \n(a/t:\n \nSilp mamkabi wals\n)\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nAsk yourself\n \n/ Pregúntate, Pregúntese\n\nMamna\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngroan, sigh, moan, wailing\n \n/ gemido, suspiro, lamentos\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n:\n \nMamna\n \nis also the 2\nnd\n \nperson\n \nconstruct form of\n \nMana\n \n/\n \nMamna\n \ntambién es la forma constr\nuctiva\n \nde 2ª persona de\n\nMana\n)\n\nMamna lulkaia\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta,bh,sln,lrw,sn,mwb\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto groan, to sigh, to moan, to wail\n \n/ gemir, suspirar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/19\n):\n \nWan mamna lulki bîla sip aisaras kabia sin, nahki tnatka ra Jehova wan walisa?\n \n–\n \nIf we are not able to\nspeak our groanings (NWT-Romans 8:26-\n“unuttered groanings”), in what way does Jehovah listen to us?\n \n/ Si no podemos\nhablar nuestros gemidos (TNM-Romanos 8:26- \"lamentos no expresados\"), ¿de qué manera nos escucha Jehová?)\n\nMamna lulkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngroaning, moaning, sighing, wailing\n \n/ gemir, suspirar\n\nMamrikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show you\n \n/ mostrarte\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMarikaia\n \n–\n \nto show\n \n/ mostrar;\n \nMairikaia\n \n–\n \nto show\nme\n \n/ mostrarme)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb-60\n):\n \nGâd naika piua ba mamrikan.\n \n–\n \nGod showed you the future.\n \n/ Dios te mostró el futuro.)\n\nMamunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente of/de:\n \nMunaia\n)\n \n–\n \ndoer\n \n/ hacedor\n\n(Construct:\n \nMamunrika\n)\n\nMamyunaia\n \n(v-irregularity of / irregularidad de:\n \nMayunaia\n; See also/ Ver también:\n \nAimayunaia\n \n&\n \nMaiyunaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto\npraise you, to worship you\n \n/ alabarte, adorarte\n\n(Note/Nota: If the object of the praise is the first person, the verb is\n \nMaiyunaia\n \n–\n \nto praise me\n. / Si el objeto del alabanza es la\nprimera persona, el verbo es\n \nMaiyunaia\n \n–\n \nalabarme\n.)\n\nMan\n \n(pron)\n \n–\n \nyou, your\n \n/ tú, vos, usted, ti, tu\n\nMan sika\n \n–\n \nit is you; it is up to you; it is yours; it is your decision\n \n/ eres tú; es tuyo; es tu decisión\n\nMan silp\n \n–\n \nyourself\n \n/ tú mismo\n\nMan\n \n–\n \nShort form of / Forma corta de:\n \nBaman\n\nManâ\n \n(\ndb,lfb\n)\n \n–\n \nmanna\n \n/ maná",
